  <section class="as-section" id="faq">
    <div class="as-wrap">
      <div class="as-intro"><div class="as-eyebrow">Questions from association leaders</div><h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2><p class="as-lead">Explore how credential infrastructure can support professional association programs.</p></div>
      <div class="as-faq-list">
        
        <details>
          <summary>What are digital badges for professional associations?</summary>
          <div class="as-faq-answer"><p>Digital badges are a visual way to recognise membership, participation, professional development or assessed achievement. A structured digital credential adds issuer information, award criteria, relevant evidence and verification. CertifyMe connects that recognition with credential management, reviewed skills relationships and professional records.</p></div>
        </details>
        
        <details>
          <summary>How can associations issue digital badges?</summary>
          <div class="as-faq-answer"><p>Create a branded credential template, define the achievement and approved recipient data, then issue individually, in bulk or through a configured API or automation workflow. Your association controls award eligibility and approval; members receive access to their credential and its sharing and verification options.</p></div>
        </details>
        
        <details>
          <summary>Can associations issue digital certifications?</summary>
          <div class="as-faq-answer"><p>Yes. CertifyMe supports digital badges and certificates representing an association&#39;s certifications. Your association defines the assessment, professional standards, issuer authority and award requirements. The credential carries that achievement into a digital record with applicable dates, status and verification.</p></div>
        </details>
        
        <details>
          <summary>Can digital badges be used for CPD?</summary>
          <div class="as-faq-answer"><p>Yes. Associations can recognise approved continuing professional development, courses, webinars, workshops and conferences with digital credentials. Include the activity, completion requirements, evidence and relevant CPD information. Your association determines credit rules and acceptance; participation alone should not be presented as assessed competence.</p></div>
        </details>
        
        <details>
          <summary>Can members share their digital badges?</summary>
          <div class="as-faq-answer"><p>Members can share credential links on LinkedIn, professional profiles, CVs, portfolios and with employers or receiving organisations. The credential provides issuer and achievement context beyond an image. Record access, disclosure and supported export formats are configured for the programme and its receiving systems.</p></div>
        </details>
        
        <details>
          <summary>How can employers verify association credentials?</summary>
          <div class="as-faq-answer"><p>An employer can open a shared credential link or use supported verification access to review the association as issuer, the achievement and applicable dates or status. Compatible verification checks supported proof and credential integrity. The employer applies its own acceptance policy; verification is not independent identity assurance or automatic licensing recognition.</p></div>
        </details>
        
        <details>
          <summary>Can associations manage certification renewals?</summary>
          <div class="as-faq-answer"><p>Credential dates, status, updates and supported revocation workflows help associations maintain certification records through renewal and recertification. Your association sets continuing education requirements, assessment, approvals and renewal decisions. Agree how the membership or certification system supplies approved changes and how renewed credentials are issued.</p></div>
        </details>
        
        <details>
          <summary>Can we automate badge issuance from our LMS?</summary>
          <div class="as-faq-answer"><p>Yes. Configured API and available automation workflows can connect approved LMS completion or assessment data to credential issuance and recipient notification. Define eligibility, evidence, data mapping, templates and approval points before enabling automation. The integration method and event handling depend on your LMS and programme.</p></div>
        </details>
        
        <details>
          <summary>Can we issue Open Badges 3.0 credentials?</summary>
          <div class="as-faq-answer"><p>Yes. CertifyMe is listed by 1EdTech as an Open Badges 3.0 certified issuer. Open Badges 3.0 uses structured achievement data based on the W3C Verifiable Credentials model. Compatibility depends on the credential profile, supported proof and receiving system; the certification does not imply universal acceptance.</p></div>
        </details>
        
        <details>
          <summary>Can badges be connected to skills?</summary>
          <div class="as-faq-answer"><p>Credentials and learning outcomes can be mapped to reviewed skills and competency frameworks, including ESCO, O*NET, association-defined models and custom frameworks. Your association determines what the achievement and assessment establish. A taxonomy relationship helps describe capability; it does not automatically prove that every member possesses a skill.</p></div>
        </details>
        
        <details>
          <summary>Can credentials be part of a Comprehensive Learner Record?</summary>
          <div class="as-faq-answer"><p>Yes. A Comprehensive Learner Record can connect credentials, skills, competencies and other achievements across a member&#39;s learning journey while retaining issuer provenance. Define which records contribute, how they accumulate, access and disclosure, and supported formats with your credential team. A professional record can continue beyond one course or certification.</p></div>
        </details>
        
        <details>
          <summary>Can we manage multiple credential programs?</summary>
          <div class="as-faq-answer"><p>Yes. Use reusable templates, multiple credential types, role-based administration, bulk or API issuance, lifecycle management and reporting across programmes. Your association defines issuer responsibilities and approval workflows so certification, CPD, events and member recognition retain consistent standards.</p></div>
        </details>
        
        <details>
          <summary>Can we brand credentials with our association identity?</summary>
          <div class="as-faq-answer"><p>Yes. CertifyMe supports credential branding and white-label experiences, including branded credential pages and email, with custom domains where supported by the configured offering. Your association remains the identified issuer. Agree designs, domain setup and delivery requirements for your programme.</p></div>
        </details>
        
        <details>
          <summary>Can CertifyMe integrate with our AMS or LMS?</summary>
          <div class="as-faq-answer"><p>CertifyMe provides REST APIs, an integration directory and available automation routes to connect approved data from existing systems. LMS integrations and AMS connections must be assessed against the specific platform and workflow. An API-based connection is not the same as a native connector; confirm the method, permissions and data responsibilities before implementation.</p></div>
        </details>
        
        <details>
          <summary>Can CertifyMe support large credential programs?</summary>
          <div class="as-faq-answer"><p>CertifyMe supports bulk issuance, API-based automation, reusable templates, role-based administration, credential lifecycle workflows and engagement analytics for larger programmes. Scope expected volumes, integrations, security, service arrangements and rollout with the platform team. A staged pilot helps validate the complete member and administrator experience before expansion.</p></div>
        </details>
        
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

